1. CSEP-Japan All Japan testing region definition
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File:      data/csep_japan/japan.forecast.nodes
Provider:  CSEP-Japan testing centre, Earthquake Research Institute,
           University of Tokyo
Obtained:  Supplied directly by the testing centre, October 2026
Content:   20,062 cell centres on a 0.1 by 0.1 degree lattice defining the
           All Japan testing region

The region specification is published in:
    Tsuruoka, H., Hirata, N., Schorlemmer, D., Euchner, F., Nanjo, K. Z., and
    Jordan, T. H. (2012). CSEP Testing Center and the first results of the
    earthquake forecast testing experiment in Japan. Earth, Planets and Space
    64(8), 661-671. doi:10.5047/eps.2012.06.007

This file is included so that the region used in this evaluation is verifiable
rather than described. Its inclusion does not imply that the testing centre,
the Earthquake Research Institute, or any person affiliated with them has
reviewed, endorsed, or is associated with this study. No such review has taken
place. Correspondence with the testing centre has been limited to factual
questions about the region file and the catalog.

