           data/jma_catalog/jma_mc_working_attrition.md
           data/jma_catalog/jma_catalog_manifest.json
           data/jma_catalog/jma_mc_working_manifest.json
           data/jma_catalog/sha256_raw.txt
Source:    Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA) Seismological Bulletin,
           hypocenter files for 2016 to 2023
Terms:     JMA website content is provided under the Public Data License
           (Version 1.0), which JMA states is compatible with the Creative
           Commons Attribution License 4.0, and which requires the user to
           cite the source and, where the content has been edited, to include
           a statement to that effect.
           See https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/en/copyright.html

STATEMENT OF EDITING, as required by those terms:

    The JMA-derived files in this repository HAVE BEEN EDITED. They are not
    the JMA Seismological Bulletin and must not be cited as it. They are
    derived products, produced by applying the nine selection rules
    pre-registered for this study to the published bulletin: a time window,
    a regional selection, a depth limit, an event-type restriction, a
    solution-quality restriction, a magnitude-scale restriction, a magnitude
    threshold, and the associated unit conversions and reformatting. Records
    were selected, fields were converted, and the output format is this
    study's own. The selection is documented in
    docs/BLOCK1_publication_target_and_region_selection_2026-11-09.docx and
    implemented in build_jma_catalog.py. Per-rule attrition over all
    2,161,892 input records is recorded in data/jma_catalog/jma_attrition.md.

    The raw bulletin archives as received are NOT redistributed here. Their
    SHA-256 values are recorded in data/jma_catalog/sha256_raw.txt so that a
    reader who obtains the archives from JMA can confirm they match the inputs
    used. Anyone wanting the bulletin itself should obtain it from JMA.

